
export const rooster = {
    introduction: `Jaunty Rooster, you were born to bounce back. Your life is a roller-coaster ride, a chaotic mix of successes and setbacks, periods of prosperity and hardship, trials, tribulations, and other emotionally draining or gut-wrenching experiences, yet you remain an irrepressibly steadfast and courageous spirit. Resilience is your defining characteristic. Regardless of the depth of despair, you simply pick yourself up, smooth your feathers, and confidently stride forward once more. You radiate enthusiasm. Your joy in experiencing new thrills is infectious. People eagerly seek your company, wishing to visit your places, see your sights, and share your exciting way of life. You will frequently hold positions of authority. You are naturally inclined to lead and excel at setting a positive example. You work exceptionally hard.

Despite a sometimes arrogant demeanor and a tendency towards conceit, you cannot be accused of being either overly aggressive or pedantic. You are a multi-talented, open-minded, yet curiously conservative individual. In matters of love, you are captivated by elegance and sophistication. Consider pursuing a glamorous Snake, or engage with an encouraging Dog. Even better, for the sake of a challenge, allow yourself to be charmed by a steady Ox. All of these pairings are capable of easing the difficulties and alleviating the strain of your exhaustingly busy life.

Listen closely. Heed my advice: you are too direct for your own benefit. Make an effort to be less candid. Your bluntness can be your downfall. Feel free to promote yourself, but try not to expose your own weaknesses in the process. Remember, a Rooster in trouble is nothing more than chicken soup.`,
    elements: {
        Wood: `This Rooster possesses a unique ability to persevere in areas where significant effort is crucial for achieving results. Its inherent vigor, conscientiousness, and meticulousness empower it to execute complex tasks that might intimidate less organized or "picky" individuals. However, do not ask the Wood Rooster to agree to spend a lifetime poring over yellowed texts in a dark attic room to produce an encyclopedic volume at the end of its life. Wood Roosters are only capable of exerting enormous effort for short-term undertakings. This individual is best suited for roles such as an efficiency expert, troubleshooter, or project manager, whose primary objective is to "get the job done well—now."

It is a sociable creature and enjoys being in friendly company where it can express itself, share some of its best stories, recount its travels, or listen attentively to the tales spun by its companions. Parties and festivals delight this naturally hospitable type, who will often host, do the cooking, purchase the wine, and (although it is far from wasteful with money) indulge its beloved guests with luxuries for the pleasure of ensuring they have a good time.

Some consider the Wood Rooster a superficial person because appearance holds paramount importance for him. It is important to understand that, on a personal level, he is preoccupied—even obsessed—with youth and fascinated by the "look" of things. Wood Roosters sincerely believe that one's appearance reflects one's essence. They cannot tolerate the idea of being old, irritable, wrinkled, or excluded from mainstream ideas. Even after middle age, the Wood Rooster is likely to continue dressing in youthful, form-fitting clothing and exert every effort to remain slender, agile, and self-assured. He seeks the company and intimacy of people younger than himself in an attempt to maintain his vitality. He often behaves in a manner not entirely consistent with his age—taking up roller-skating at forty, purchasing rock music at sixty, and dancing at seventy in noisy discos where no one else has yet reached their twentieth birthday.

As talkative and sociable as this creature is, the Wood Rooster has a significant emotional block when it comes to expressing his feelings. He can converse extensively about anything he considers polite conversation. In private, however, on subjects deeply personal to one’s heart and soul, he remains completely uncommunicative. If you love one of these emotionally reserved individuals, you will face a considerable challenge trying to encourage him to articulate what is on his mind. Whether this Rooster is angry or sorry, sad, glad, or madly, passionately in love, his exterior remains cool, sleek, well-groomed, nervous, and rather too serious. The Wood Rooster is the type of emotionally constrained person to whom it is necessary to ask a hundred times a day, "Do you love me, darling?" or "Honey, are you angry with me?" They require profound emotional events and insistent, heartfelt lovers to help them open up. Unless the Wood Rooster learns to directly address his feelings, an unhealthy accumulation of anger and resentment will almost certainly remain with him and his intimates for the rest of his days.`,
        Fire: `Complexity! And passion. Fire illuminates the Rooster in peculiar, exaggerated ways, causing him to be born tormented, difficult, and fiery! Fire Roosters are volatile, craving confrontation and confidently rushing from one head-on collision to another without sustaining so much as a tiny scratch.

This Rooster seems to thrive on exhilaration. He is enthusiastic about and involved in everything. Monotony and a lack of challenge bore and depress him. He desires to be right in the midst of the action, on the front lines. Regardless of how tough the dare, he will gladly undertake it. His capacity for work is monumental. His endurance is legendary. His cutting-edge brilliance at absorbing information is staggering. And, finally, his ability to organize others at work while still retaining their respect and affection is top-tier. Fire Roosters were born to be world-beaters, but, unfortunately for them, Fate simultaneously cursed them with a built-in emotional instability.

Fire Roosters should be more successful than they typically are. They are relentlessly ambitious, intelligent, and competent individuals. They make excellent lawyers, caring doctors, innovative scientists, and capable business people. However, because emotions play a primary role in how these individuals conduct business, they often create confusion. Whether they are deeply involved in a conference, eloquently presenting facts in a court case, or reciting crucial figures at a bankruptcy hearing, Fire Roosters remain vulnerable to emotional involvement. They can be swayed into submission if the boss’s wife has had a miscarriage, feel sympathetic because the accountant is overweight, or distort their plea because the other lawyer’s husband just lost his job—anything emotional that enters the Fire Rooster’s mind during business hours poses a potential danger to the outcome of his efforts. Objectivity eludes him.

This person is impulsive, headstrong, and cannot be easily reasoned with. Conjugal life with a Fire Rooster is a testament to friction and very often becomes explosive to the point of being unbearable. He can be tyrannical and despotic, too, especially if his pride is offended. The Fire Rooster believes strongly in absolute rightness and earnestly desires the truth to be revealed. But if voicing the truth involves revealing his own vulnerability or letting down his guard, the Fire Rooster may simply refuse and miss the point entirely: his promises are often little more than promises. He’s emotionally fragile, needing to be liked as well as to enjoy the thrill of victory. He fails because he's conflicted. He doesn't want to apply the rules of ruthlessness to his own advancement, yet because he is so intellectually gifted for clarity, he can perfectly well discern what is necessary to succeed.

On the positive side, the Fire Rooster is a fabulous friend, an amusing companion, and an honest, truthful colleague. In social settings, he enjoys his role as a non-conformist and is sometimes even exhibitionistically bohemian to make a point. He possesses a sound sense of morality, but will not go out of his way unless you go out of yours to champion causes or perform good deeds. He is a tit-for-tat person whose love of honesty and talent for being brutally frank carries him cheerfully along on the crest of his own enthusiasm. He falters when he confronts emotional imperatives with which he cannot reason. But, because he is a Rooster, even repeated failures and torrential setbacks do not deter his courage or dampen his spirit. He was born to bounce back.

As he is easily labeled puritanical in his approach to sex, this deeply troubled Rooster might be better off living in a cloister, adopting some ascetic course of action that does not demand emotional involvement. When effectively utilized, the Fire Rooster’s richly nuanced emotional capacity can produce excellent creative results. But if he chooses to become an artist, he will require both isolation and protection from the outside world.`,
        Earth: `A powerful intellect combined with a flair for the aesthetic, feminine side of life bestows upon this Rooster a talent for nuance and creativity that surpasses that of his more conventional Rooster brothers and sisters. Because of his gift for conversation, some find the Earth Rooster exasperatingly vague and accuse him of not sticking to the point when he delivers rambling speeches. His ability to engage with abstract concepts allows him great verbal freedom, but for those who value concrete facts, his mental meanderings can seem incomprehensible. There's no need to worry, however: this Rooster also has a firm grasp on factual information.

His thought processes can best be described as "penetrating," and his critical abilities as "dead accurate." When he needs to be precise, an Earth Rooster always gets straight to the point, recalling every single detail and date of what occurred previously. He will never allow his interlocutor to get away with fudging even a single detail. It's almost as if, to counteract his own tendency towards vagueness, he feels compelled to be ruthlessly factual in his recollections. Earth Roosters possess elephantine memories, minds like steel traps, and enough common sense to manage both Hungary and Yugoslavia single-handedly.

This is an uncommonly elegant person of regal bearing whose sense of humor—a twinkle, a wink, or a swift, ambiguous glance—always shines through his slightly forbidding facade. It is his great fortune to possess excellent health and frequently to live to a great age. Not only does he live a long time in good condition, the Earth Rooster ages gracefully, retains his agile, quick wit, and rarely suffers symptoms of senility. I know three 1909 Roosters and am certain that today any one of them could tackle a battery of the demanding exams we set our eighteen-year-olds. Earth Roosters grow old with poise, remaining steadfast and individualistic, but shedding the anxiety of their troubled youth to become serene and accepting.

The Earth Rooster only reaches his optimal performance once he has found true love. As he is somewhat timid in youth, he doesn’t always dare to be forward with the opposite sex. An air of naive embarrassment may deter others from attempting to seduce this reserved, conservative creature. He is unlikely to bring home some fleeting lover picked up at a singles bar, usually becoming involved with someone met through a cousin or at a family gathering or wedding. They often marry later than their peers, and because they choose carefully and wait for the right person, they rarely get divorced.

Sexual passion is not the strong suit of this deeply loving person. No tender pats on the head, overt signs of affection, poetic love letters, or exotic love potions for this no-nonsense individual. The Earth Rooster prefers to keep love pure and sensible, never allowing his pristine image to become muddled with sentimental scenes or sticky with emotion.

To succeed professionally, Earth Roosters require a support network. Working for a family business or a large corporation suits them, as they always enjoy playing an integral part in a communal effort. These individuals make excellent accountants, bankers, doctors, architects, and designers. They are meticulous with details and non-impulsive. Although they may experience some tough financial patches, Earth Roosters do not usually go bankrupt or lose their fortunes through foolish investments.`,
        Metal: `Here is a creature born to be on the stage, in the movies, or simply in the middle of his own living room, putting on a show for his family. The Metal Rooster is a performer, the life and soul of the party. People either like this fervent person immensely or find it difficult to tolerate him. Metal Roosters are sometimes boastful: they enjoy promoting themselves, sharing their success stories and those of their family, and generally letting you know how wonderful they are. Although this trait can be tiresome, the Metal Rooster’s purpose is neither egotistical nor greedy. He doesn’t want to impress anyone because he needs or wants something from them. Rather, it is part of his flamboyant nature. Although some find it irritating, others, because this person is usually funny and imaginative, adore being invited to witness the daily spectacle and manage to live happily ever after with this incorrigible entertainer.

If he doesn’t learn to temper it while young, this brash, confident person’s tongue can get him into trouble throughout his life. He is incapable of diplomacy and has a way of blurting out indelicate truths at the most inopportune moments, encountering failure and rejection where he might have found success and approval. When criticized for being too candid, the Metal Rooster may erupt into a short-lived fit of defensive rage. He isn’t the type to bear a grudge. But, given his inclination for speechmaking, his verbose outbursts of bad temper can be impressive enough to cloud an otherwise sunny afternoon.

The Metal Rooster loves organization: he needs to keep things neat and tidy—a place for everything and everything in its place. He doesn’t like to be interrupted when devising new tricks or engaged in his favorite hobby. He cannot tolerate having too much improvisation imposed upon him.

All of the above somewhat fastidious traits may cause a Metal Rooster to spend his adult life alone, without a full-time partner, children, or pets to disrupt the life he has so meticulously planned.

Roosters hold conservative political opinions. They make excellent policemen and, as they crave movement, thrive on travel, and enjoy being expatriates, may find lucrative, secure positions with organizations such as the FBI or Interpol. Of course, their inherent indiscretion might hinder their progress in jobs requiring top-secret classifications. But the Metal Rooster is intelligent and, with a little help from his friends, can certainly learn how to keep quiet in life-or-death circumstances.

The Metal Rooster is perfectly suited for jobs in theater, cinema, and TV. If he does not choose to perform, he should try to become involved in production. When he succeeds in this challenging profession, he will certainly have many fans and followers who will cheer him on and keep his career advancing. He is a natural for stand-up comedy routines, as a talk-show host, and might make a superb newscaster, roving reporter, and even war correspondent.`,
        Water: `Here we encounter the exceptionally multi-talented Rooster. Possessing all the most significant Rooster strengths and weaknesses combined, the Water Rooster might be considered the quintessential model for all other Roosters. He is serious. He is resolute and meticulous. He talks about himself quite a bit. He meticulously cares for his appearance as well as his wardrobe. He is a willing traveler and adores adventure. He knows how to work diligently and persistently to achieve a goal. He endures many setbacks, yet no matter how far he falls behind financially, this Rooster can always discover a new way to earn a living from nothing.

There are, however, a few distinct characteristics about the Water Rooster that set him apart. He is exceptionally adaptable. He’s not rigid but does hold conservative views on almost everything—except his rather inconsistent pattern of fidelity—which he accepts as his inherent right and privilege. Ironically, the Water Rooster is also jealous and possessive of his lovers and mistresses. For him, a double standard applies. Why? Because he says so. Water Roosters either get to be the boss, or they pack their bags and go home.

The Water Rooster loves to be surrounded by people. The more individuals who contact him on any given day, the happier he becomes. He actively seeks out the company of friends and family and will go to great lengths to succeed. He entertains frequently and is often an excellent cook and host. Possibly because he is so eager for companionship, he may, at times, lend assistance to someone less scrupulous than himself. If he is not careful, he may be exploited by ruthless individuals who profit from his goodwill and offer nothing in return.

The Water Rooster is thin-skinned. He cannot tolerate being advised, interfered with, or—heaven forbid—reprimanded. Even if he knows he has made mistakes or is about to encounter significant trouble, he does not wish to be reminded or warned of it. His reactions are not positive to even the mildest suggestion on how he might alter his approach or modify his thinking. If you don’t want to lose his friendship, do not attempt to play truth games with the Water Rooster. If you dare to utter one piercingly true statement in his presence, he’ll become unpleasant and hostile. He may only sulk for a period, but he might never call you again.

Essentially, the Water Rooster suffers from an inferiority complex. He often wishes that he were someone more fortunate whose parents had left him a fortune, a network of influential contacts in the world, or, even better, a chain of supermarkets to call his own. This Rooster often carries a chip on his shoulder about the injustices he feels society has committed against him, but, as he will not listen to the truth about himself nor squarely face his real place in the world, he often has to confront failure, which exacerbates his inferiority complex. As he grows older, this cycle of events becomes increasingly detrimental. If he cannot lower his guard and learn to accept advice, he may become so disgruntled that, by middle age, he may be permanently embittered, withdrawing from society and life as a cheerful hippie or a homeless person.

Despite his unflagging energy and industriousness, the Water Rooster secretly desires to be wealthy. He often envisions himself in a luxurious environment where satin sheets are commonplace and silk pajamas are essential. He even dreams of ample leisure time to recline and read novels and philosophical texts. Roosters are not adept at being idle, as they become bored when they have too much free time. Therefore, this period of idleness usually remains merely a dream.

It is not the Water Rooster’s destiny to become rich overnight. If he marries a wealthy woman whose father owns the biggest construction business in town, the old man will almost certainly go bankrupt the week after the wedding or die and leave all his money to some charity. If he enters into some get-rich-quick business deal where he feels certain to make a fortune in a week, the Better Business Bureau may shut him down or someone will report on TV that his products are defective. The Water Rooster is born to labor. He is both talented for and fated to earn a living from the most barren ground and, above all, to persist day after day, building a solid financial foundation until he has amassed a fortune. His lot may be demanding, but it is nothing to be ashamed of.

Water Roosters possess a seductive quality. Not only are they excellent conversationalists, but they also have a charming way with words that makes them irresistible as salespeople, lovers, advertisers, politicians, and teachers. Loving one of these masterful Water Roosters is a full-time commitment. They do not like to be left alone and cannot tolerate idleness. They require adoration and praise—but even if they receive more than their fair share of compliments, they still may not always be faithful to their partner.`,
    },
    compatibilities: {
        "Rat": "This is a relationship to be avoided at all costs for both parties. The Rat’s need for control and tendency to meddle clash disastrously with the Rooster’s proud, independent nature. The Rat seeks to dominate, offering unsolicited advice and attempting to organize the Rooster’s life, which the Rooster finds suffocating and intolerable. The Rooster’s bluntness and tendency to speak out of turn wound the Rat’s sensitive ego, leading to constant arguments and mutual resentment. Initially, there may be a spark of attraction, as the Rat admires the Rooster’s confidence and the Rooster is drawn to the Rat’s cleverness. However, this quickly fades as their differences surface. The Rat’s secretive, calculating nature frustrates the Rooster, who values honesty and directness. Meanwhile, the Rooster’s flamboyant self-promotion irritates the Rat, who prefers subtlety and discretion. Financially, they are at odds: the Rat hoards resources, while the Rooster spends freely on appearances and social status. Romantically, this pairing is a disaster. The Rat’s need for emotional security is unmet by the Rooster’s emotional reserve, and the Rooster feels smothered by the Rat’s possessiveness. Sexual compatibility is low, as the Rat craves intimacy that the Rooster is unwilling or unable to provide. Both parties are better off seeking partners who complement their strengths rather than exacerbate their weaknesses. This relationship is a recipe for frustration and heartbreak.",
        "Ox": "This is a match made in heaven for the Rooster, who finds in the Ox a steady, reliable partner that brings calm to their chaotic life. The Ox’s patience and methodical nature complement the Rooster’s energetic, ambitious spirit, creating a balanced and harmonious relationship. The Ox admires the Rooster’s hard work and leadership qualities, while the Rooster appreciates the Ox’s loyalty and lack of interference. There’s no power struggle here—the Ox is content to support the Rooster’s endeavors without meddling. Financially, this pair is a powerhouse. The Ox’s frugality and the Rooster’s discipline ensure a stable, prosperous future. They share a conservative outlook, valuing tradition and security, which aligns their goals. The Ox’s serene presence helps the Rooster slow down and reflect, adding depth to their otherwise materialistic tendencies. In return, the Rooster’s enthusiasm injects energy into the Ox’s steady routine. Romantically, the Ox provides the unconditional love the Rooster craves, though the Rooster must be careful not to take advantage of the Ox’s devotion with reckless behavior. Sexual intimacy is not overly passionate but is grounded in mutual respect and trust. The Rooster’s flamboyance is tempered by the Ox’s simplicity, making for a stable, long-lasting partnership. This is one of the Rooster’s best matches, promising both emotional and financial security.",
        "Tiger": "The Rooster and Tiger form a dynamic, if challenging, friendship, but a romantic relationship between them is fraught with difficulties. Both are bold, energetic, and independent, which creates an initial spark of mutual admiration. The Tiger respects the Rooster’s resilience and confidence, while the Rooster is drawn to the Tiger’s adventurous spirit. However, their similarities breed conflict, as both crave the spotlight and resist being overshadowed. The Tiger’s impulsive, free-spirited nature clashes with the Rooster’s need for structure and order. The Rooster’s blunt critiques wound the Tiger’s pride, while the Tiger’s tendency to leap into risky ventures frustrates the Rooster’s conservative sensibilities. Financially, they struggle—the Tiger’s recklessness with money conflicts with the Rooster’s careful budgeting. Their home life is chaotic, with constant debates over lifestyle choices and priorities. Romantically, passion is high, but so is instability. The Tiger’s need for freedom chafes against the Rooster’s desire for control, leading to frequent arguments. Sexual chemistry is intense but short-lived, as neither can sustain the emotional intimacy needed for a lasting bond. While they may enjoy each other’s company as friends or colleagues, a romantic partnership is likely to burn out quickly unless both learn to compromise—a tall order for these headstrong signs.",
        "Rabbit": "This pairing offers the Rooster a calm, supportive environment to thrive in, as the Cat/Rabbit’s gentle, refined nature complements the Rooster’s energetic drive. The Cat/Rabbit is content to stay out of the Rooster’s way, allowing them to pursue their ambitions without interference. The Rooster’s hard work and dedication impress the Cat/Rabbit, who admires their discipline and leadership. In return, the Cat/Rabbit’s artistic, introspective qualities inspire the Rooster to explore their creative side. Financially, this pair can succeed if the Rooster takes charge of budgeting, as the Cat/Rabbit tends to be less practical with money. Their shared appreciation for beauty and refinement creates a harmonious home life, filled with art, music, and elegant surroundings. The Cat/Rabbit’s patience soothes the Rooster’s occasional irritability, while the Rooster’s enthusiasm prevents the Cat/Rabbit from becoming too withdrawn. Romantically, this relationship is stable but not overly passionate. The Cat/Rabbit’s reserved nature aligns with the Rooster’s emotional restraint, though the Rooster may crave more excitement. Sexual intimacy is gentle and affectionate, reflecting their mutual respect. The Rooster must avoid being too critical, as the Cat/Rabbit is sensitive to harsh words. With mutual care, this pairing can foster a peaceful, productive partnership that supports the Rooster’s ambitions and the Cat/Rabbit’s creativity.",
        "Dragon": "The Rooster and Dragon form a vibrant, mutually inspiring partnership that thrives on shared energy and ambition. Both are dynamic, confident, and love the spotlight, creating a relationship filled with excitement and celebration. The Dragon’s flamboyant, charismatic nature invigorates the Rooster, while the Rooster’s discipline and work ethic ground the Dragon’s grand ideas. They complement each other beautifully, with the Dragon dreaming big and the Rooster executing plans with precision. Financially, this pair can achieve great success, as the Dragon’s boldness attracts opportunities and the Rooster’s meticulousness ensures they are capitalized on. Their home life is lively, with frequent social gatherings and a shared love for luxury and festivity. The Dragon’s hands-off approach allows the Rooster to shine without feeling stifled, while the Rooster’s loyalty keeps the Dragon grounded. Romantically, this is a passionate match. The Dragon’s intensity sparks the Rooster’s enthusiasm, leading to a fiery, committed relationship. Sexual chemistry is strong, fueled by mutual admiration and a desire to impress each other. The only risk is if the Rooster tries to outshine the Dragon, which could lead to ego clashes. As long as both respect each other’s need for attention, this pairing promises a thrilling, successful union.",
        "Snake": "This is a near-perfect match for the Rooster, who finds in the Snake an elegant, sophisticated partner that complements their own flair for style and ambition. The Snake’s charm and social grace captivate the Rooster, while the Rooster’s hard work and resilience impress the Snake. Their shared love for refinement and tradition creates a harmonious partnership, with both valuing a well-organized, aesthetically pleasing life. Financially, they face some challenges. The Snake’s tendency to spend lavishly clashes with the Rooster’s frugality, leading to potential arguments. The Rooster should take charge of finances to maintain stability, though the Snake may resist. Romantically, their chemistry is strong, with the Snake’s sensuality igniting the Rooster’s passion. The Snake’s ability to teach and guide in the bedroom helps the Rooster overcome their emotional reserve, leading to a fulfilling sexual connection. The main hurdle is the Snake’s occasional promiscuity, which the Rooster’s conservative nature finds difficult to accept. If the Snake can curb their wandering tendencies and the Rooster can avoid harsh judgments, this pair can build a lasting, elegant partnership. Their social life will be rich, filled with glamorous events and mutual admiration, making this one of the Rooster’s most compatible matches.",
        "Horse": "If there is one thing the Horse hates more than anything, it’s being held back or restrained in any way. The Horse is a doer, an active person with more irons in the fire than a roomful of blacksmiths. They are a runner, a worker, and a striver. Nobody should ever attempt to hold them down. Yet, in this relationship, the Horse must live with the Rooster’s firm grip on their pocketbook and disapproval of their wildest dreams. Roosters are serious, single-minded individuals; they cling to conservative ideas and prefer the traditional to the outlandish in life. The atmosphere of this pairing inclines both to adhere to rules, be thrifty, and stick to tried and true methods. The Horse might be tempted to travel afar to visit tombs and museums, churches, temples, and monuments, as the Rooster doesn’t usually disapprove of travel—especially if the journey leads to somewhere instructional and is not just for 'fun.' Major purchases (houses, cars, boats, buildings, farms, etc.) are not advisable in this relationship, as money will be generally tight and interest rates quite high. The Horse’s favorite outspoken and outrageous extreme behaviors should be curbed. Romantic indiscretions are also not advisable for Horse people with Roosters.",
        "Goat": "This relationship is a delightful blend of creativity and discipline, with the Rooster and Goat complementing each other’s strengths. The Goat’s artistic, free-spirited nature captivates the Rooster, who admires their grace and charm. In return, the Rooster’s hard work and organization provide the stability the Goat often lacks. Together, they create a synergistic partnership, with the Rooster grounding the Goat’s dreams and the Goat adding beauty to the Rooster’s structured life. Financially, this pair struggles, as both are prone to extravagance. The Rooster’s discipline can help, but the Goat’s love of luxury may lead to unpaid bills. The Rooster must take charge of budgeting to avoid conflict. Romantically, their connection is strong, with the Goat’s seductive allure drawing out the Rooster’s passion. Sexual intimacy is vibrant, as the Goat’s sensuality encourages the Rooster to loosen up. The challenge lies in the Goat’s need for dependency, which the Rooster may find burdensome, and the Rooster’s bluntness, which can hurt the sensitive Goat. If the Rooster can be patient and the Goat can embrace some responsibility, this pair can build a beautiful, passionate life together, filled with art, love, and mutual support.",
        "Monkey": "This pairing starts with promise but often falters due to fundamental differences. The Rooster is drawn to the Monkey’s charm and versatility, while the Monkey admires the Rooster’s dedication and confidence. Their shared charitable tendencies create an initial bond, as both enjoy helping others. However, their contrasting approaches to life soon cause friction. The Rooster’s need for structure and elegance clashes with the Monkey’s casual, spontaneous nature. The Rooster finds the Monkey’s lack of refinement frustrating, while the Monkey grows bored with the Rooster’s deliberate pace. Financially, they struggle, as the Rooster’s careful budgeting conflicts with the Monkey’s indifference to money. Communication breaks down, as the Rooster’s bluntness offends the Monkey, and the Monkey’s evasiveness irritates the Rooster. Romantically, their sexual chemistry is strong, with the Rooster’s passion igniting the Monkey’s playful side. However, emotional intimacy is lacking, as the Rooster struggles to open up and the Monkey avoids deep conversations. This relationship works best as a friendship or professional partnership, where their differences can be managed, but as a romantic union, it often fizzles out due to incompatible lifestyles.",
        "Rooster": "This couple faces significant challenges at best, as their inevitable conflicts over various issues, ranging from finances to clothing styles and choices of schools for their children, are almost never worth the effort to resolve. What we observe here are two opinionated, ego-centric individuals. They are, first and foremost, their own worst enemies and require more cheerful, compliant partners than either can be for the other. Roosters need to be comforted and gently persuaded. It is highly unlikely that any Rooster would agree to coax another—unless in a dire situation where the other Rooster was a fallen comrade. The metaphor of war is fitting. Each Rooster involved in a Rooster/Rooster pairing desires to be the General. Each needs to feel superior to the other. Each is conservative and reserved, uncertain of their own image, yet fiercely spirited. Daily battles rage, viciously tearing harmony to shreds. Roosters often form friendships with each other. They think similarly and share comparable views. They can even collaborate professionally—provided one is willing to take a less prominent role. However, romantic love between Roosters rarely results in equilibrium. Their sexual intimacy is lukewarm: neither is capable of expressing passion without assistance from a more vigorously self-assured partner.",
        "Dog": "Incompatibility reigns supreme in this couple. Dogs and Roosters are equally resolute and sensitive. Dogs are constantly blurting out criticisms and bruising the egos of those around them. Roosters are confident but deeply insecure. A single harsh remark from the Dog’s repertoire of biting bluntness can incapacitate the Rooster for days, causing depression and undoing his hard-earned image. Do these individuals fight? They never cease. Backbiting, complaining, bickering over minor details. They disagree on everything. Dogs are typically left-wing, compassionate, and trustworthy. Roosters are inherently conservative individuals who believe in the system, adhere to society’s fundamental principles, and cling to traditional ways. This couple’s home life is a constant tug-of-war of political unrest. The Dog desires revolution. The Rooster devoutly wishes for the status quo. The Dog believes mismatched china and a floor pallet will suffice. The Rooster wants fine porcelain or Limoges china set with crystal glasses on an heirloom table. The Dog wants to spend money on causes. The Rooster wants to keep his money in the bank. The Rooster demands more frequent and varied sexual activity than the Dog is willing to provide. The Rooster needs to inflate his ego and preen his feathers. The Dog couldn’t care less about his appearance in bed; he experiences sex rather than performing it. Besides, Dogs are slightly puritanical; they do not believe one should overindulge in pleasure. It is best to leave the Rooster/Dog romantic relationship alone.",
        "Pig": "This partnership has the potential to succeed brilliantly. Roosters who find themselves intimately involved with willing, sensual Pigs are truly fortunate. My advice to this lucky Rooster is to hold on tight: you will not find such amiability, charm, and easygoing devotion anywhere else in the zodiac. Pigs are willing to adapt and change, modifying their personalities and lifestyles to suit the one they love. With all your ups and downs, resounding successes and failures, you will definitely benefit from the presence of a kind, nurturing, understanding Pig. As for the Pig in this relationship, you will gain much from the pure discipline and frank style of a Rooster partner. Roosters prefer things as they are; they are not revolutionaries. Pigs, too, enjoy tradition and respect the basic tenets of a good society. Your common interests will flourish, and after the first few years, this will lead you very far towards achieving dreams and goals you only envisioned before meeting. Sexual intimacy, too, is favored in this couple. The Rooster can take charge in lovemaking. Pigs appreciate being guided to exotic heights in bed, adore almost anything sensual, and make excellent cuddling partners for the often unrefined Rooster to learn to snuggle with. If I were a Rooster, I think I might seek a Pig mate. Your lifelong happiness and financial security (Pigs attract money) would be assured.",
    },
    futures: {
        "2025": { "year": "Snake", "element": "Wood", "prediction": `This year is a good one for you. You will continue to experience a carefree disposition, finding a fresh sense of luxury and social acceptance as this Snake year concludes. Snake individuals are not known for being the most outgoing people. However, they frequently prefer the gentle, artistic companionship of Goats. You are currently operating on your unique frequency, pursuing your activities at a notably unhurried pace. Your calm and deliberate approach appeals to the Snake, who favors navigating life effortlessly and without urgency. Your relaxed companionship brings comfort to the otherwise reserved Snake. Anticipate receiving invitations to numerous elegant dinner parties and events in exotic locations, possibly even on yachts or at chateaux in France or Spain. Prepare your most luxurious car, enhance your wardrobe, and remember to apply the finest French colognes and other sophisticated cosmetics. Naturally, all this personal grooming and socializing will present you with a multitude of romantic opportunities. You will be pursued by such a diverse array of new individuals that you will find it difficult to keep count. Savor these experiences while they endure, as romantic pursuits will come to an abrupt stop by the year's end. If you are considering marrying one of your romantic successes, I advise you to reconsider. Marriage is not yet foreseen for you.` },
        "2026": { "year": "Horse", "element": "Fire", "prediction": `By this point, after all the recent events, your romantic life should have recovered (and you should be feeling more confident). One characteristic Roosters often exhibit is a reluctance to listen. You operate, manage, and execute tasks with efficiency. You stay vigilant and adhere to your timetable. However, you occasionally miss opportunities because you believe you possess all knowledge and prefer not to encounter new information that might overwhelm your thoughts or compel you to alter your established routines. Pay close attention. The Horse year represents an ideal period for those who are intensely dedicated to work. You are an individual who thrives on demanding tasks. Even if you were retired, you would still be actively engaged in something. This could involve cooking, simultaneously reading three books, gardening, jogging, building, or even shopping. You are a versatile individual who enjoys being involved in numerous activities and projects. Your energetic disposition perfectly complements the Horse’s temperament. If you persist in advancing so eagerly with all your projects, you will encounter no impediments to progress this year. Minor family disagreements may emerge periodically during Horse years. You are unable to resolve them, so do not exhaust yourself by attempting to. A loved one might experience an illness. Offer your presence and support. Hold their hand and offer gentle, comforting words. There is nothing quite like strong support from a reliable Rooster friend to uplift one’s spirits. Increase your protein intake and reduce your sugar consumption.` },
        "2027": { "year": "Goat", "element": "Fire", "prediction": `The Goat possesses a level of creativity far exceeding your expectations. Goats navigate life quite effectively through intuition and improvisation. They enjoy the freedom to frolic and feed in fertile areas that, ideally, are not even their own property. You Roosters approach most aspects of life with extreme seriousness—especially your financial matters. Consequently, the unpredictable nature and general atmosphere of this Goat year do not particularly appeal to you. Indeed, it causes you considerable irritation. You might wonder why accomplishing tasks is so challenging this year, why no one adheres to schedules, or why timetables were changed, requiring you to work overtime without respite. You might even question who disrupted your established routine. You might express your displeasure through grumbling, complaining, muttering, and moaning. However, rest assured, it will not alter the situation. The Goat finds comfort amidst disorder. Particularly chaos that it has created itself. You become distressed in chaotic circumstances and yearn for order to be re-established immediately. Regrettably, you will not be able to have things your way this year. And failing to get what you desire tends to unsettle you. You might spend a significant portion of this Goat year in a state of agitation. My recommendation? Deliberately reduce your pace. Consider taking a mild sedative. Prioritize more sleep and cease worrying about what cannot be remedied. Your romantic partner will assist you in relaxing and approaching things with more ease. And if they are unable to soothe your anxieties, consider seeking psychiatric help.` },
        "2028": { "year": "Monkey", "element": "Earth", "prediction": `This Monkey year might provoke your temper even more intensely than the Goat year did. Monkeys are reasonably organized and generally succeed in adhering to routines. However, they are also prone to deception. Monkeys skillfully maneuver situations and individuals to achieve their desires. You Rooster individuals prefer straightforward, simple communication and direct action. You accomplish tasks by personally undertaking them. The Monkey operates differently. The Monkey achieves its objectives and resolves issues through indirect and not always honest means. And if Monkeys can persuade others to resolve matters on their behalf, they will do so. Therefore, throughout this Monkey year, you will continue to complain. However, your irritability won't stem from delayed trains or altered schedules. You will simply lament the necessity of interpreting subtle cues to comprehend the events of this turbulent year. Rather than being able to calmly discuss and finalize a budget at a conference table, you will be compelled to remain vigilant for hidden agendas among your colleagues and partners. Even your personal life will be overshadowed by the feeling that certain information is being withheld from you. Confidential information is being guarded. This atmosphere of unspoken trickery will irritate you. While your nerves were undoubtedly frayed last year, this year might prove to be more challenging. You will experience a sense of disorientation—like a deer caught in headlights. You will ponder, "What exactly is happening here?" Continue to question. However, persevere. Next year, your life will significantly improve.` },
        "2029": { "year": "Rooster", "element": "Earth", "prediction": `Yippee! This is your very own year to take charge, to direct people, to get them organized, and to enforce all the rules. It was certainly time you received some relief from the last two disorderly years and were able to set things right. You will need to monitor your expenditures carefully this year, as Rooster years tend to be like that. However, you don’t mind maintaining detailed accounts and watching every penny as it leaves your purse. What you do mind is being forced to allow less competent individuals to give you orders when you know perfectly well how best to manage yourself. Do remember that this year you must sit down quietly somewhere to contemplate and plan the next twelve years of your life. Every twelve years, we are obligated to create a plan. How do you intend to construct the next phase of your existence? How do you envision living out the years ahead? What are your primary goals? You have reached your current age and have begun to wonder what actions you can take to improve your situation. The significant question to ask yourself is, "What do I truly desire?" Then, begin to imagine where you wish to be in twelve years. How will you live? With whom? Where? If financial prosperity is your aim, create a business plan and adhere to it. If love is what you seek, start actively looking for the person to share your life with. If you aspire to be an artist, take concrete steps to achieve that. Year by year, make lists of your objectives and then (because you are so adept at following routines) make the necessary adjustments in your current life to align with your future.` },
        "2030": { "year": "Dog", "element": "Metal", "prediction": `Rooster survival often depends on enduring a series of exhilarating roller coaster rides. You ascend and descend every breathtaking hill and valley, expressing your feelings loudly. But you always emerge smiling, once again earning money and enjoying a good life. In Dog years, there is considerable resistance towards individuals who accumulate wealth. The Dog embodies justice for all. He desires his subjects to engage in causes, take up arms, and march through the streets demanding reforms in all social programs. The Dog makes life more pleasant for those who join him in demonstrations and agree with his plans to improve the circumstances of everyone. You, of course, might participate in a protest march against war or against tax increases. However, I don’t envision many Roosters at rallies advocating for homeless shelters or demanding equal healthcare for everyone. You are too much of an individualist to join forces with a group of overly compassionate liberals. You simply desire a peaceful life where the dates on your calendar remain consistent year after year and do not have to signify poverty marches one year and immigration rallies the next. This year, I suggest you stay out of contentious situations. Do not let the Dog catch you accumulating too much money, or he may compel you to finance his campaign for educating all of Africa. The Rooster’s journey is ascending the first hill this year. Slow but steady progress is guaranteed.` },
        "2031": { "year": "Pig", "element": "Metal", "prediction": `Where the Dog might take pride in having "plenty of nothing," the Pig is delighted to offer us an abundance of everything. You needed a break, and this year provides exactly that for Roosters. Your to-do list will diminish as the year progresses because there is absolutely no obstacle on the horizon. You will not only enjoy the sense of security and prosperity that characterizes this Pig year, but you will also take pleasure in the more boisterous aspects of life. Pigs are known for their virtue, good taste, and purity of heart. However, they are also prone to expressions of excessive sensuality. Pigs frequently tell off-color jokes. Other people might have landscape paintings in their bedrooms; Pigs have nudes. Pigs watch adult films and access erotic content on the Internet. I agree that virtue juxtaposed with sensuality is an unusual combination, but it is very real. Pigs are a little bit "piggy" when it comes to sexual matters. This does not shock or offend you Roosters. You might not be the type to recount a crude joke, but if one is told in your company, you may just laugh heartily and ask for more. In light of the Pig’s inclination for the sensual, you or your significant other may be tempted to stray this year. If your lover confesses a minor infidelity, please do not feel obligated to retaliate by committing one of your own. Forgive, but do not forget.` },
        "2032": { "year": "Rat", "element": "Water", "prediction": `Reduce your extravagant habits. Stop believing you can simply and cheerfully travel anywhere you please, spend a few days enjoying yourself in Paris, Marrakech, or Bali, and still emerge unscathed. You Roosters are not very flexible and tend to corner yourselves. If you’re working, then the job becomes the sole focus of your thoughts and actions. You obsess, overwork, and burn out very quickly. Then, naturally, you feel sorry for yourself and decide you are owed a break. But once again, instead of simply resting and reading a thick novel for a couple of days at home, you feel compelled to move about. So you jet off to precisely the place you desire, with the ideal climate, the most delicious food, and the best people. Then, as soon as you arrive, you begin spending all the money you earned while overworking and burning out. Is this beginning to sound like a recurring pattern? Well, the Rat year is a favorable period for you Rooster individuals… but only if you break this frantic pattern of yours and embrace rest and relaxation within your own surroundings. For heaven’s sake, sit still. Take breaks during the day to attend yoga classes. Meditate. Practice Tai Chi or take Pilates courses. And instead of spending your hard-earned, burnout-induced cash on air travel and wine, deposit a significant amount in the bank and allow it to earn you some interest. Slow down, or risk serious consequences.` },
        "2033": { "year": "Ox", "element": "Water", "prediction": `The Ox is your most significant supporter. In fact, if you have not yet become romantically involved with one of these stabilizing creatures, you have missed the last opportunity for paradise. Oxen have a calming effect on Roosters. Their serene influence reduces the Rooster’s usual high velocity by half, allowing for introspection and self-realization. Since you Roosters typically do not favor deep thought and are almost never interested in anything more profound than a new outfit, an impressive house, or a gourmet meal, the presence of the Ox this year helps to add depth to your excessively materialistic considerations. This year, you may discover that there is more to life than material possessions. Love is in the air, and in this relationship, you are the "beloved"—meaning the other person is profoundly fond of you. Because you are so certain of this unconditional affection, you tend to imagine that you can get away with all sorts of unpredictable behavior (affairs, flirting, spontaneous weekends away, etc.). Be more gentle. The lover in question is beginning to learn to establish boundaries, and you may lose him or her to someone far sweeter and more attentive. You would do well to order some exquisite flowers and tickets to a tropical island paradise for two, or your loved one may become restless. Money will be plentiful. However, stop acquiring more possessions anyway. Refrain from all clothing purchases—not because it’s wasteful—but because you genuinely do not need to own thirty pairs of designer jeans.` },
        "2034": { "year": "Tiger", "element": "Wood", "prediction": `For Roosters, the Tiger can be a friend and even a close companion. However, Tigers move around a great deal, and they move rapidly. Roosters are certainly not slow-paced; yet, they will find it incredibly challenging to keep up with Tiger associates this year. Of course, you cannot withdraw now, so the most effective strategy will be to accelerate your pace or risk losses—both financial and personal. It is not merely the dizzying speed that perplexes Roosters in Tiger years. It is also the multitude of changes imposed upon them by the unpredictable, tawny creature. Roosters are individuals who adhere to schedules, enjoy structure, and cling to order. Moreover, Roosters require a certain degree of comfort. They may appear audacious and seem capable of adapting quickly. But in reality, although they often love to journey to and explore distant lands, Rooster-born individuals are quite conservative in their travel choices. You won't find many Rooster individuals hiking with backpacks in Patagonia or cycling a thousand miles through rugged terrain to help eradicate poverty. However, Tigers enjoy adventures, both elegant and challenging, and if they become passionate about a cause, they can and will traverse a thousand miles of rock and river to help eliminate poverty. Therefore, this year, Roosters should be prepared to accept changes in routine, upheaval at work and at home, and setbacks both large and small. Maintain the rhythm, and you will succeed. Slow down, and you will be outrun by Tiger competitors of every kind.` },
        "2035": { "year": "Rabbit", "element": "Wood", "prediction": `Feeling relieved to be out of the frenzied Tiger year, all Roosters will be able to breathe more freely this year. The refined and delicate Cat/Rabbit feels neither strongly positive nor negative about you, and will, for the most part, stay out of your way. Since you are not one to disrupt established situations or create unnecessary disturbances, you are welcome this year to advance your own projects and will, if you apply yourself as diligently as you usually do, make significant progress. As the atmosphere surrounding you is less chaotic than last year, you can actually think clearly and are not afraid of slowing down lest you be ambushed by some unexpected disaster. Your romantic prospects remain unexciting. But there's no need to worry; next year promises to bring you both passion and commitment from someone you can genuinely envision living with. Meanwhile, you should utilize the tranquility of this Cat/Rabbit year to resolve any outstanding financial issues and address the more complicated problems burdening your family. Intruders may attempt to damage your property this year. Invest in an alarm system or acquire a large dog to guard your home. There is also a slight possibility you may be defrauded of a substantial sum of money. If you take precautions with all new people you meet, work with, or employ (by checking their background and assessing their capabilities in the workplace), you should be able to avert this danger.` },
        "2036": { "year": "Dragon", "element": "Fire", "prediction": `The Dragon inspires you. You find its intensely energetic nature invigorating. You are also an energetic individual, but your strength is resolute, and your demeanor is more stoic. The Dragon, by contrast, is all flamboyance and exuberance. He is constantly hosting parties, inviting people off the street to celebrate any holiday. And if there isn’t a holiday, he or she will invent one for the occasion. You will certainly be among the guests at most, if not all, of these gatherings. Enjoy yourself! But do remember that there is work to be done. You might consider starting a new business or opening a few branch offices of your existing business. You will also be earning more money: new capital, new energy, and new love in your life! This person will probably be someone you never imagined meeting—someone quite unlike your usual type. If you always preferred short, well-built men with curly hair, this one will be a tall, thin, bald older gentleman. If you always dated shallow blondes with long legs, you will fall madly in love with a short, dark-haired beauty with intellect. Whatever you were accustomed to, this year will bring the opposite. This individual will not only infuse your life with profound passion, but he or she might even become a potential life partner. Proceed slowly. Make no commitments until eighteen months have passed. Do you promise?` }
    }
};
